---
---

<section class="section" id="partners">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Page 3 — For Partners</p>
      <h2>Built to be adopted, not just admired.</h2>
      <p class="partners-intro">Whether you're a studio or school interested in Cadenza, an investor evaluating the pitch, or a team building on Curator's gateway to shareable offline AI infrastructure, here's the case for working with us.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pitch-section">
      <div class="pitch-layout">
        <div class="pitch-text">
          <h3>The Pitch in Sixty Seconds</h3>
          <p>Every school and studio sits on knowledge it owns but can't safely hand to cloud AI — lesson records, student files, policies, community archives. Curator is open, local-first AI infrastructure that lets those organizations run intelligent workflows on their own knowledge, on hardware they own. Our first application, Cadenza, gives music teachers back the hours they lose to administrative overhead after every lesson. Cadenza is the wedge; Curator is the platform every studio, school, and archive will need next.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pitch-video">
          <video
            controls
            preload="metadata"
            style="width: 100%; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); box-shadow: 0 2px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);"
          >
            <source src="/videos/why-local-first.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--ink-muted); margin-top: 0.5rem;">Why Local-First AI Is EdTech's Future</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="investor-section">
      <h3>What an Investor Is Actually Buying</h3>
      <div class="investor-grid">
        <div class="investor-card">
          <h4>Data and Business Independence</h4>
          <p>Data staying local is becoming an increasingly important concern as institutions rely more on private cloud tools. Curator is built on the idea that private retention of a business's data should be a natural preference and institutional norm.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="investor-card">
          <h4>A Wedge Into the Offline SaaS Market</h4>
          <p>Making Cadenza freely available lets individuals determine whether the technology is worth it for their own business. This approach dramatically lowers customer-acquisition costs, allowing teachers and developers alike to find ways to use the technology or build their own use cases on top of the existing Curator engine.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="market-section">
      <h3>Where Curator Sits in the Market</h3>
      <div class="market-table">
        <div class="market-row market-row--header">
          <span class="market-cell"></span>
          <span class="market-cell">Cloud AI suites (e.g. NotebookLM)</span>
          <span class="market-cell">Generic admin SaaS Tools (e.g. MyMusicStaff)</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Curator</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Where data lives</span>
          <span class="market-cell">Third-party cloud</span>
          <span class="market-cell">Centralized cloud server</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Your building</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Where the AI runs</span>
          <span class="market-cell">Centralized servers</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No AI available</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Your hardware</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Understands your lesson content</span>
          <span class="market-cell">General models only</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Yes, against your library</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Drafts real work</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Yes, queued for approval</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Works without internet</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Yes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Inspectable source code</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Open core</span>
        </div>
        <div class="market-row">
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--label">Deployable under your own brand</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell">No</span>
          <span class="market-cell market-cell--highlight">Yes</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="market-note">Comparison describes the typical architecture of each category; individual products vary.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="business-section">
      <h3>How the Business Works</h3>
      <p>Curator's monetization strategy focuses on the friction it removes as offline networks become interdependent, rather than on the owner's documents and information. By designing for users to self-host on hardware they already own, we've made it possible for teachers and developers to adopt the software at zero cost to us. Letting clients choose between their own hardware configuration or a self-contained, pre-configured Curator Node removes technical barriers for those who may not be familiar with installing software, by providing a plug-and-play headless server for those who'd rather not manage it themselves. By bundling premium features alongside our open-source software releases, we can entice users to subscribe to additional features such as secure file sharing between networks and encrypted backups.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pilot-section">
      <h3>The Plan to Prove It</h3>
      <p>The first pilot cohort will consist of 8–10 independent music studios or private music teachers, running Cadenza free for six months in exchange for an honest testimonial.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="pushback-section">
      <h3>Where We Expect Pushback</h3>
      <div class="pushback-grid">
        <div class="pushback-item">
          <p class="pushback-q">"Couldn't ChatGPT or NotebookLM just add an offline toggle?"</p>
          <p class="pushback-a">Their business models run on centralized compute and data. Offering a true offline-first AI suite of administrative tools that complements existing workflows and processes keeps our processes offline and eliminates the need for external tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pushback-item">
          <p class="pushback-q">"Institutional investment might take 18 months or longer. How do you plan to survive that unpredictability?"</p>
          <p class="pushback-a">Our initial goal was never to start there. We want to land with individual teachers who adopt offline-centric tooling and open-source software directly so their engagement remains organic and natural. Sustained interest in our SaaS solution will be what eventually pulls the product beyond horizontal market application towards vertical growth opportunities beyond individuals and music studio infrastructure.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pushback-item">
          <p class="pushback-q">"What happens when the AI hallucinates and gets something wrong?"</p>
          <p class="pushback-a">Given the design of our offline infrastructure, nothing will ever send itself automatically. The role of Curator is only to generate drafts and analyze based on its own sources. Further to that, a human approves every message, invoice, and record change before it reaches a client, keeping the software "human-first."</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pushback-item">
          <p class="pushback-q">"The market is crowded."</p>
          <p class="pushback-a">Our approach sits one layer up from many of the competitors that focus solely on online tooling.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .partners-intro {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .pitch-section, .investor-section, .market-section, .business-section, .pilot-section, .pushback-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
  }
  .pitch-section h3, .investor-section h3, .market-section h3, .business-section h3, .pilot-section h3, .pushback-section h3 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .pitch-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 3fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .pitch-text p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .pitch-video {
    max-width: 320px;
  }
  .pitch-video video {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .investor-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .investor-card {
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }
  .investor-card h4 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }
  .investor-card p {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .market-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .market-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 180px repeat(3, 1fr);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .market-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .market-row--header {
    background: var(--surface);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .market-cell {
    padding: var(--space-md);
    border-right: 1px solid var(--border);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .market-cell:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .market-cell--label {
    font-weight: 600;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .market-cell--highlight {
    background: rgba(232, 115, 47, 0.06);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent-orange);
  }
  .market-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-light);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .pushback-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .pushback-item {
    padding: var(--space-xl);
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .pushback-q {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .pushback-a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .investor-grid, .pushback-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .pitch-layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .market-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .market-cell {
      border-right: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
  }
</style>
